\label{fig:overtime}
\end{figure}

The two seasonal patterns are shown directly in Figure~\ref{fig:season}. Sales
peak on Mondays and are lowest on Saturdays. Most stores are closed on Sundays;
the few that open, mostly Type~B, have high sales, so the Sunday bar reflects
those stores rather than a typical Sunday. The monthly profile shows the pronounced
December effect consistent with Christmas shopping. This strong, repeating
structure is the predictable component $\delta_{s,t}$ that a store mean cannot
capture but a day-of-week baseline and the trees can.

\begin{figure}[htbp]
\centering
\begin{subfigure}{0.48\textwidth}\centering
\IfFileExists{eda_outputs/fig_eda_dow.pdf}{\includegraphics[width=\textwidth]{fig_eda_dow.pdf}}{\fbox{\parbox{0.9\textwidth}{\centering\vspace{1em}[fig\_eda\_dow]\vspace{1em}}}}
