The four store types differ in average level, in opening policy, and in how much
of their variation is weekly. Table~\ref{tab:storetypes} summarises them.
Type~B stores are open on almost every Sunday, record average sales well above
the other types, and carry the largest weekly-predictable share, the proportion
of within-store variance explained by store-specific day-of-week means. This
makes them the most predictable group and is what drives the store-type
experiment in Section~\ref{sec:subsets}.

