\subsection*{Reproducibility}
The source is \texttt{Kayra\_Isik\_thesis\_final\_v3.Rnw}. Every table and
summary plot is drawn from machine-readable result files. The audit file
\texttt{table\_provenance.csv} records the executed report or CSV behind each
archived result. These archived results are not presented as one new,
synchronised rerun of the full panel, and differences between repeated
specifications are kept with their source. The covariate-matched comparison is
reproduced by \texttt{rossmann\_arimax.Rmd} and the training-history check by
\texttt{rossmann\_arimax\_history.Rmd}; their samples, predictions, model
orders, uncertainty calculations and session details are kept. The six-month
diagnosis in Section~\ref{sec:subsets_results} is reproduced by
\texttt{rossmann\_window6\_diagnostic.Rmd} from the saved six-month fit. A failed fit
cannot silently drop a store, and a missing result table stops compilation.
Earlier versions of the code are available at
\url{https://github.com/kayraisik/Rossmann-M5_thesis}.
